# OCI 11.2's execute of a block with two associative arrays.
# Captured 2026-11-08 through tools/capture_proxy.py: an OCI 11.2 program
# (instant client 11.2, x86-64 Linux; OCIBindByName with maxarr_len and curelep)
# on Oracle 11g XE 11.2.0.2, of BEGIN zz_probe_arr.go(:a, :s, :n); END; with :a
# a NUMBER array IN (10, 20, 30), :s a VARCHAR2 array IN OUT ('ab', 'cde') and :n
# a NUMBER OUT. The TTC payload, without the packet's header, as `hexdump -C`
# output; the offset column and the |ascii| gutter are ignored by
# tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
